# Secrets & Config

## Purpose

Keep privileged secrets out of the client and real authorization in the backend.

## When Applied

Touching config, keys, environment wiring, or auth/RLS-adjacent code.

## Requirements

- **Forbidden in the Flutter app:** Supabase `service_role`, any privileged server secret, hard-coded private tokens.
- **Allowed:** publishable/anon key via `--dart-define` (`lib/core/config/supabase_config.dart`). Prefer env/`dart-define` over expanding checked-in defaults.
- Admin role checks in the client are UX only — RLS + RPCs enforce real authorization.
- FCM tokens live on `profiles.fcm_token`; clear on sign-out.
- Public payment-screenshot URLs are intentional but sensitive — don't broaden public buckets casually.
- See [`docs/security-notes.md`](../../../docs/security-notes.md).

## Examples

```bash
flutter run --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
```

## Anti-patterns

- Committing a `service_role` key or embedding it for "admin features".
- Weakening RLS so the client can skip a check.

## Common Mistakes

- Hard-coding keys as defaults instead of `dart-define`.
- Trusting a client-side `role` flag as authorization.
